**F1 — CONFIRMED — medium**

Location: `scripts/checks/lib/stack_bound.py:227`; dynamic counterpart: `scripts/checks/lib/stack_access.py:40`.

Reproducer input and command:

```bash
printf '0000000000401000 <main>:\n  401000: mov byte ptr fs:[0x100000], 0x0\n  401009: ret\n' > fs.dis
python3 "$R/scripts/checks/lib/stack_bound.py" x86_64-linux fs.dis
```

Observed output: `bound 0`, exit 0. Calling `x86_addresses()` on that same memory operand returned `[]`.

An FS base of `main_entry_sp - 0x100080` places the effective write at `main_entry_sp - 128`, despite the FS base itself being outside the stack.

Structural cause: segment-relative offsets are exempted without constraining their effective addresses.

