**F7 — CONFIRMED — high**

Location: `scripts/land/train.sh:513` for the head; line 523 for members. The verifier accepts a syntactically valid base at `scripts/review/verify.sh:56` without checking coverage.

For temporary history A→B→C, the only review note was on C:

```text
verdict: clean
rounds: 2
reviewer: codex
utc: 2026-11-08T00:00:00Z
base: <B>
pieces: 1
```

Commands:

```bash
bash "$R/scripts/review/verify.sh" "$C"
# Extract and source the current review_provenance function.
VERIFY="$R/scripts/review/verify.sh"
REMOTE=.
review_provenance probe "$C"
```

Observed: verifier exit 0 with `base <B>`; provenance exit 0 with:

```text
the head 4ef5728a12 carries a clean review note
```

A train starting at A therefore accepts a note covering only B..C, leaving A..B unreviewed.

Structural cause: provenance binds the head SHA but never requires review coverage back to the train base.

